\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

\textbf{Research Questions.}
\textbf{RQ1:} \emph{QoE--stall Pareto front} --- does the catastrophic-ratio knob $\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}$ trace a non-trivial Pareto front, and does the VMAF-aware fallback Pareto-dominate uniform-decrement projection at matched rebuffer budgets?\;
\textbf{RQ2:} \emph{Baseline competitiveness} --- where do the recommended operating points of the Pareto family sit relative to RobustMPC and Pensieve in the (QoE, Rebuffer) plane?\;
\textbf{RQ3:} \emph{Component ablations} --- isolated value of future-aware lookahead, Lyapunov-style cues, and Lagrangian dual updates inside the constrained policy.\;
\textbf{RQ4:} \emph{Shield-design space structure} --- across $\VShieldVariants$ shield variants, do behaviors collapse into a small number of equivalence classes, and which inference-time mechanisms add measurable headroom?\;
\textbf{RQ5:} \emph{Policy/shield co-design} --- to what extent do constrained-trained policies depend on having a shield available at inference?

\textbf{Procedure.} Multi-video trace-driven emulator (four evaluation videos, FCC/Norway-style partitioned traces consistent with codebase paths~\cite{fcc2015mba,kvalbein2014}); each episode spans \(K_e{=}48\) chunk decisions with fixed \(T_{\mathrm{c}}\) as in Sec.~\ref{sec:system}; deterministic evaluation policies; Pensieve reproduced with observation masking for fairness. All shield comparisons hold the underlying policy and trace seeds constant and only vary inference-time shield parameters, enabling paired statistical pairing across operating points.
\textbf{Table~\ref{tab:main:results}} summarizes 80 paired episodes (\(4\times20\)) aggregated means from policy-mode harness logs (exported CSV in the artifact repository beside the plotting script). Companion scripts regenerate publication PDF/PNG figures and excerpt \LaTeX{} table fragments bundled under \texttt{new/src/paper/}.

\textbf{Reporting integrity.} Genie~\cite{mao2017neural} leverages non-causal perfect trace knowledge and is included only as an oracle reference. We therefore do not treat Genie as a deployable competitor when interpreting statistical comparisons.

